* The proportion of direct plans in total SIP AUM has increased over the last five years, from 12% in March 2020 to 21% in March 2025.
* There is a shift towards long-term wealth creation strategies, with the ratio of SIP assets held for more than five years increasing substantially, while the ratio of SIP assets held for less than one year has decreased significantly.

Overall, the data suggests that investors are embracing disciplined, long-term investing, and SIPs are becoming an increasingly popular investment avenue.
