Investors embrace long-term approach with SIPs 
The proportion of direct plans in total SIP AUM has increased over the last five years from 12% as of March 2020 to 
21% as of March 2025. 
The ratio of SIP assets held for more than five years , as of March 2025 vis -à-vis March 2020,  has increased 
substantially, indicating a shift towards long-term wealth creation strategies 
In contrast to direct plans, r egular plans have a significantly higher proportion of SIP assets held for more than five 
years. Also, the proportion of SIP assets held for less than one year in regular plans has decreased sharply compared 
to the decrease in direct plans. 
