More than half of India's MF assets concentrated in top 5 cities 
As of March 2025, the top five cities – Mumbai, New Delhi, Bengaluru, Pune, and Kolkata – collectively account for 
over half (52.52%) of the country's MF AUM. Mumbai holds 27%, New Delhi 12.63%, Bengaluru 5.39%, Pune 4% 
and Kolkata 3.49%. This distribution is consistent with the previous year's trend.  
