Global Overview 
In the US, debt MF AUM surged by 6.7%, reaching $5,169.7 billion as of March 2025, up from USD 4,845.3 billion in 
March 2024. In contrast, equity mutual fund AUM saw a marginal 0.16% increase to USD 14,408.5 billion, while 
hybrid AUM declined by 0.77% to USD 1,592.8 billion from $1,605.2 billion over the same period. 
Investments into debt mutual funds (excluding money-market funds) surged in the US in fiscal 2025. The positive 
flows amounted to USD 1,02,740 Mn. Conversely, equity and hybrid funds both saw net outflows during the year 
amounting to USD 717,595 Mn and USD 118,128 Mn respectively.  
Rate cuts by the US Federal Reserve and expectations of further  cuts, global trade wars and significant policy 
changes by the newly elected government prompted investors towards safer investments to mitigate risks associated 
with market uncertainty. 
